Phase 7 item 4 (scheduled and event-triggered tasks on the daemon) — E2E proof
Date: 2026-09-11

Scope proven (real SQLite store v11, real command processor, production dispatch):
1. CreateAutomation RPC (29): durable spec in the automations table;
   exactly-one-trigger rule (cron XOR event_pattern); cron specs VALIDATED
   AT CREATION (unparsable spec refused with a typed error — never
   registered dead). ListAutomations RPC (30) returns spec + fire state.
2. Cron engine: boundary-keyed firing (UTC minute "YYYYMMDDHHmm") — a
   matching minute fires EXACTLY once across ticks AND restarts
   (last_fire_key recorded, asserted in the ListAutomations response);
   a second tick in the same minute is a no-op. Minimal 5-field cron
   parser (lists/ranges/steps, Sunday 0-or-7, day-of-month/day-of-week
   cron semantics) verified against calendar-checked fixtures
   (2026-09-07 Monday / 2026-09-12 Saturday cross-checked via dow).
3. Event engine: event_pattern automations consume the durable event
   stream past a persisted rowid watermark — task_completed fired one
   follow-up task; a re-tick NEVER double-fires (watermark proof).
4. Fired tasks are REAL tasks: created AND queued through the same
   CommandProcessor path (state asserted 'queued', task aggregate
   asserted), actor = the automation id (audit trail).
5. Daemon wiring: modbit-core spawns the engine thread (30s cadence,
   SystemTime-driven tick).

Test evidence: cargo test -p modbit-core-runtime --lib automation +
--test agent_fleet_e2e (cron_automation_fires_a_real_task_exactly_once_
per_boundary, event_automation_follows_task_completion_without_double_
firing; 9/9 in the file, full workspace 548 tests 0 failed).

